==Enemy==
R.Ost is among the most well-equipped pushers in the game. He has somewhat fast movement speed, high health, enough range to hide behind most peons, and rapid, hard-hitting Area Attacks that will shred your cats. The icing on the cake is his 10%  [[Critical Hit]] chance which makes fighting him much more inconsistent. Fortunately, he doesn't have too much range, and he has five knockbacks which reduces his heavy pushing power.

At high strength magnifications (200% or above) R.Ost will out-perform similar bosses like [[Bore]]s and [[Teacher Bun Bun|Bun Buns]], as there are very few consistent [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|Traitless counters]] working against them. In mixed stages, he may disrupt whatever strategy you are using to take down the Traited enemies. The bottom line is that if there is an R.Ost on a stage, you need to account for it.

==Strategy==
Long-ranged attackers such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]], ([[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed]]) [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] and/or [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]] will do fine against R.Ost in earlier stages. However, in much later encounters, you may need the use of more [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-control]] against R.Ost. [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]] and/or [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Glass Cat]] can be good at this, as long as using crowd-control is not exploitable by the other enemies in the stage. Another, less applicable strategy for R.Ost is to use Awakened Bahamut Cat. When used correctly, he can chip off an R.Ost by being timed to strike during R.Ost's backswing animation (the second peck), then let the R.Ost be finished by the rest of your attackers if Awakened Bahamut Cat did not kill said R.Ost. For this to work, Awakened Bahamut Cat must approach while R.Ost is frozen or during R.Ost's backswing and there can't be any other enemies in front of R.Ost. Freeze effects, such as the [[Ototo Corps#Thunderbolt|Thunderbolt Cannon]] and [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]], can make this easier to time and give more chances. Unfortunately, this tactic becomes less and less viable at higher magnifications where R.Ost could destroy Bahamut in two hits (or instantly with a Critical Hit) and has enough health to avoid being knocked back in even one, so you should mostly rely on your usual counters. And although R.Ost's fast attacks make it seem very hard to stall without crowd controller units, it is actually pretty vulnerable to meatshield spamming. At least 4 meatshields can pretty much stall R.Ost for a decent amount of time.

Some units exclusive to the [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] event will do very well against this avian atrocity, and [[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Jagando]] & [[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]] can deal with them in the late game. The [[Weaken|weaken]] effect helps a lot too, so don't be afraid to save an extra slot for [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge Cat]]. Overall, this enemy is not very difficult when alone, but can be a real pain in numbers (e.g. in [[The Bathroom]], [[Procrastinator Parade]], and [[Caliban's Keeper]]) or with enemies that take advantage of his many knockbacks, such as [[Hannya]] in [[Realm of Carnage (Deadly)|Realm of Carnage]] and [[Wrath of Carnage (Deadly)|Wrath of Carnage]].

A strategy for stalling groups of R.Osts is to use [[Suntan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Suntan Cat]], as the fast attacks will usually make it so that Suntan Cat will get at least one dodge off, allowing your defenses to stay alive longer.

