==Variants==
{{Variant
|original = R.Ost
|Pure Gold R.Ost
|A [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemy introduced in the [[GOLD RUSH#The Midas Touch|Golden Week]] event. It has the usual Metal ability of only taking 1 damage except for Critical Hits, but it has much lower stats all across the board and cannot perform Critical Hits itself.
|M. Ost
|The [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] variant of R.Ost, with even higher health, damage, range and speed, but double the knockbacks. Instead of doing Critical Hits, M. Ost has a 100% chance to [[curse]], [[knockback]] and [[slow]] cats with each hit.
|Oldstrich
|The [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]]/[[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] variant of R.Ost. Unlike M. Ost, whose abilities and knockbacks often make him less of a threat than R.Ost, Oldstrich is practically a full upgrade, having 1.6M HP, 23k AP, 40.5k DPS, 300 range and infinite revives with none of M. Ost's drawbacks, on top of having 1 less knockback and higher speed than R.Ost. The 10% Critical chance is replaced with a 20% chance for a 20% [[Toxic]] attack.
|Commander Ostromeda
|The [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] variant of R.Ost. Similar to a 200% R. Ost in terms of base stats, with 290 range. Despite not being a [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Alien]], they have a 15% chance to [[warp]] cats back by 800 range for 6.7 seconds.
|Poultrio
|The [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]]/[[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]]/[[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] variant of R.Ost, introduced in the [[:Category:Advent Stages#Great Advent Stages|Great Advent Stage]] [[Invasion of Poultrio]]. Has 3.6M HP and over 33.3k DPS, moves incredibly fast, and has a chance to generate an [[Explosion]] and [[Knockback|knockback]] cats on each of the three hits of its attack. It also has a 60k HP [[Shield]] that regenerates with full HP on each of its 20 knockbacks, on top of having [[Base Destroyer]].
}}

